            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0568" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12863: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-20T16:00:00+08:00">November 20, 1934—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 20—6:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>532. Reference Legation’s 514, November 8, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="77" xml:id="d378-f1"
                    /> following has been received from the Consul General at Hankow: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“November 20, noon. In view of capture of Yungshun northwestern Hunan by
                            Ho Lung and his advance on Yuanling have advised all Americans in
                            western Hunan to evacuate. Americans have returned to Chenhsien southern
                            Hunan since main body of Reds has moved further west and there are now
                            some 15,000 troops in that city.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
